\name{InterMetaGeneChord}
\alias{InterMetaGeneChord}
\alias{print.InterMetaGeneChord}
\title{Shared Metabolic Gene-Pair Chord Diagram}
\description{
Expands one selected pathway interaction into the shared prognostic metabolic
gene pairs retained by \code{InterMetaEnrich()}. Arrows point from the gene on
the favorable-pathway side to the gene on the unfavorable-pathway side.
}
\usage{
InterMetaGeneChord(
  resdata = NULL,
  select = 1L,
  condition = "Adjust.P.Value",
  color = NULL,
  transparency = 0.4,
  label_cex = 0.8,
  start_degree = 180,
  draw = TRUE
)

\method{print}{InterMetaGeneChord}(x, ...)
}
\arguments{
  \item{resdata}{Data frame returned by \code{InterMetaEnrich()} with
  \code{keep_gene_pairs = "shared"} or \code{"all"}.}
  \item{select}{Exactly one enrichment \code{Index} identifying the pathway
  interaction to expand.}
  \item{condition}{Numeric enrichment column shown in the diagram title.}
  \item{color}{Optional gene-sector colors. An unnamed vector must contain one
  color per displayed sector. A named vector must cover the internal sector
  names, such as \code{"F::GENE"} and \code{"U::GENE"}. Deterministic warm
  and cool palettes are generated by default.}
  \item{transparency}{Chord transparency from 0 to 1.}
  \item{label_cex}{Positive text-size multiplier for gene labels.}
  \item{start_degree}{Starting angle in degrees.}
  \item{draw}{Whether to draw on the current base graphics device. Set to
  \code{FALSE} to inspect the prepared data without drawing.}
  \item{x}{An object returned by \code{InterMetaGeneChord()}.}
  \item{...}{Additional arguments ignored by the print method.}
}
\details{
The function is the metabolic-pathway counterpart of the legacy
\code{TimiGeneChord()}, which was separate from \code{TimiCellChord()}.
\code{Shared.MGP} is split into directional gene pairs, and every retained
pair is drawn with equal width. Source and target copies of the same gene use
different internal sector identifiers, so their pathway-side meaning remains
unambiguous.

Compact precomputed enrichment objects may omit \code{Shared.MGP}. If the
selected row reports shared pairs but does not retain their identifiers, the
function stops with instructions to rerun
\code{InterMetaEnrich(..., keep_gene_pairs = "shared")}. The global circular
plotting state is cleared after drawing, including when plotting fails.
}
\value{
Invisibly returns an object of class \code{InterMetaGeneChord} containing the
selected enrichment row, parsed directional \code{edges}, gene-sector
\code{nodes}, exact \code{order}, \code{group}, and \code{color} mappings,
selection metadata, pair counts, and the optional \pkg{circlize} layout.
}
\examples{
\dontrun{
library(InterMeta)
data("InterMetaExampleEnrich")

pdf("gene_pair_chord.pdf", width = 9, height = 9)
gene_chord <- InterMetaGeneChord(
  InterMetaExampleEnrich,
  select = InterMetaExampleEnrich$Index[1],
  condition = "Permutation.FDR"
)
dev.off()

print(gene_chord)
}
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{InterMetaEnrich}}, \code{\link{InterMetaPathwayChord}}
}
\keyword{hplot}
